//@version=6
// WAR FORMATION E66 — THE SHORT LEG ON THE PROXY DIRECTION RULE, NOT THE RAW 6H COLOUR.
//
// QUEUE ITEM 1 (STRATEGY-LEDGER.md HARD LESSON 32, item 2; EXPERIMENT-LOG.md queue after E65a/b):
// E64 ran the bidirectional cascade ORACLE-RULES L179-180 prescribed, as two separate legs off the
// reproducible parent e58a:
//   E64a SHORT, direction = 2+ consecutive RED 6h candles (the source's OWN literal rule):
//        PF 0.45442725 / DD 10.97440232% / 43 trades / 6.98% win.
//   E64b LONG,  direction = 2+ consecutive GREEN 6h candles (the control, source's own rule):
//        PF 0.95884068 / DD 10.63382724% / 28 trades / 35.71% win.
// NEITHER WAS KEPT (RATCHET v2 clause 1). The decomposition is the finding: going from e58a's proxy
// direction rule to the source's raw 6h count costs PF twice over — once for the direction rule itself
// (1.240 -> 0.959 on the long control) and again for the leg (0.959 -> 0.454 on the short). Both drops
// are real and separate. ORACLE-RULES L215-216 calls the straight 6h-candle count "simpler and better
// specified" than the 4-green-1h proxy; measured, it is simpler and WORSE.
//
// WHY: "4 of the last ~6 1h candles green [red]" is a PERSISTENCE condition across the whole 6h block.
// "2 consecutive 6h candles green [red]" is satisfied by two barely-green [barely-red] blocks with no
// requirement that the move persisted inside them. The proxy demands more of the regime; the source's
// raw count demands less.
//
// SO: this build is the short leg on e58a's OWN proxy direction rule — 4+ RED 1h candles inside the
// PRIOR completed 6h block (cntPrev>=5 gate, redPrev>=4), the exact mirror of e58a's bullRegime/
// greenBull logic, NOT E64a's consecutive-6h-candle count. It isolates the leg against a direction
// rule already shown to work (e58a's long, PF 1.240), rather than one just shown to underperform
// (E64's raw 6h count). The source rule is NOT adopted and NOT discarded on this one 4.5-month window
// — e58a's proxy remains the reference build either way.
//
// MECHANICS: identical mirror of E64a's short geometry (brokeAbove = 15m sweep to a higher high, THEN
// a rejection crossunder back below it) — the same "let the enemy finish" location solve ORACLE-RULES
// L175-177 requires before a short may be symmetric with the long (LESSON 6, scoped by HARD LESSON 31:
// governs geometries this project invents, not a mirror the source itself prescribes and this proxy
// already earns on the long side). Only the DIRECTION SOURCE changes from E64a: proxy 1h-persistence
// count instead of raw 6h colour. shieldUsd/maxBars/rr held EXACTLY at e58a's values (HARD LESSON
// 28/29: shield and hold cap are coupled, changing either alongside the direction rule would confound
// this run — named in advance, not discovered after).
//
// PARENT: e58a (pine/e58a-shield1000-maxbars6480.pine), CONFIRMED REPRODUCIBLE (E58=E59), PF
// 1.24015239 / DD 9.82519609% / 36 trades (long, proxy direction). This is the correct parent per the
// mandate's own instruction: the best-PF, largest-sample, lowest-DD of the three confirmed-reproducible
// ALCM families, and the one whose direction rule this leg now mirrors.
//
// PRE-RUN AUDIT, one line per item:
//   R (LESSON 3) — shieldUsd = $1,000, ~1.0% of BTC price at ~$100k, PASSES the 0.8% floor. LIVE
//        TENSION, unchanged from e58a/E64a: falls BELOW the floor above ~$125k BTC. Real over this
//        window's price range, not a formality — flagged, not hidden.
//   Stop placement (LESSON 5) — risk-defined by the shield (fixed $ gap to liquidation), the spec's
//        own exit model and the DECLARED deviation from a structural stop. No trailing, no averaging
//        down (position_size can only move toward flat, never widen against a loss).
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6, scoped by HARD LESSON 31) — SHORT ONLY. e58a's long stands alone
//        and is not re-run or blended here. Location solved structurally (brokeAbove + rejection),
//        not assumed — see MECHANICS above.
//   BINDING (E17) — bearRegime (proxy: cntPrev>=5 and redPrev>=4) must actually fire or the direction
//        rule is inert; trade count against e58a's 36 and E64a's 43 is the evidence, reported below
//        either way.
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) — bearRegime (1h persistence) and h1Bear (current 1h close < open) could proxy
//        each other. Kept because e58a's own long keeps both (regimeReady/bullRegime AND h1Bull) and
//        this run's only stated change is the direction SOURCE, not the term list — changing the term
//        list too would confound which change moved the number. If trades collapse toward zero, h1Bear
//        is the first term to drop, registered here in advance (same prediction E64a made and did not
//        need — E64a returned 43 trades, non-degenerate — so this is a lower-probability branch here).
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) — 1h green/red counts latch only on a completed 1h close (cntCur/
//        redCur roll into cntPrev/redPrev only at new6, mirroring e58a exactly); brokeAbove sets on a
//        completed 15m block; shortTrig crossunder fires on a later 1m bar. No shared-bar leakage.
//   OCCUPANCY (LESSONS 24/28/29) — a different direction rule AND a different leg both admit a
//        genuinely different trade population than e58a's 36 longs or E64a's 43 shorts. NOT a
//        controlled comparison against either. Named in advance, not discovered in get_trades after.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no martingale. Position ends at target or at the shield.
//
// PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (LESSON 17), read against BOTH e58a's long (PF 1.24015239, 36 trades) and
// E64a's raw-6h short (PF 0.45442725, 43 trades) — neither alone is decisive (LESSON 16):
//   * PF >= 1.0 with a usable count (>=20, LESSON 12) -> the short leg EXISTS under a direction rule
//     that already works on the long side. The proxy, not the leg, was E64a's problem — a major
//     finding, and the first source-faithful short to clear parity in this project's history.
//   * PF improves over E64a's 0.454 but stays below 1.0 -> the persistence proxy helps the direction
//     term (as it did for the long, 0.959->1.240) but the short leg still does not clear parity; the
//     mechanics, not the direction rule, are the remaining open question.
//   * PF at or below E64a's 0.454 -> the proxy fix that helped the long does nothing for the short;
//     the direction rule was never this leg's binding constraint, and the location solve (brokeAbove +
//     rejection) itself needs revisiting, not the direction source feeding it.
//   * Trades collapse toward single digits -> redPrev>=4 and h1Bear are the redundancy suspect (see
//     REDUNDANCY above); not read as an edge result either way (LESSON 19).
//   * Fewer than ~20 trades but not degenerate -> reported as a COUNT and a direction, not a validated
//     result, per the mandate's own restatement of the 4.5-month single-regime limit.
strategy("War Formation E66 proxy-direction SHORT", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

redBear   = input.int(4,     "Red 1h candles in PRIOR 6h block for BEAR (proxy, mirrors e58a greenBull)")
skipOpen  = input.int(60,    "Skip first N minutes of 6h block")
skipClose = input.int(60,    "Skip last N minutes of 6h block")
velK      = input.float(0.8, "Velocity: min rejection as multiple of atr(30)")
midLo     = input.float(400, "Whole-number middles low")
midHi     = input.float(600, "Whole-number middles high")
shieldUsd = input.float(1000,"THE SHIELD: fixed dollar gap to liquidation -- held at e58a value")
rr        = input.float(2.0, "Reward:risk")
maxBars   = input.int(6480,  "Max bars in trade -- held at e58a value")

MS6H = 21600000
MS1H = 3600000
MS15 = 900000

b6  = math.floor(time / MS6H)
b1h = math.floor(time / MS1H)
b15 = math.floor(time / MS15)

new6  = b6  != b6[1]
new1h = b1h != b1h[1]
new15 = b15 != b15[1]

var float h1o     = na
var int   redCur  = 0
var int   cntCur  = 0
var int   redPrev = 0
var int   cntPrev = 0

if new6
    redPrev := redCur
    cntPrev := cntCur
    redCur  := 0
    cntCur  := 0

if new1h
    if not na(h1o)
        cntCur := cntCur + 1
        if close[1] < h1o
            redCur := redCur + 1
    h1o := open

regimeReady = cntPrev >= 5
bearRegime  = regimeReady and redPrev >= redBear

minsIn   = (time - b6 * MS6H) / 60000
timeGate = minsIn >= skipOpen and minsIn <= (360 - skipClose)

h1Bear = not na(h1o) and close < h1o

var float c15h = na
var float p15h = na

if new15
    p15h := c15h
    c15h := high
else
    c15h := na(c15h) ? high : math.max(c15h, high)

brokeAbove = not na(p15h) and c15h > p15h

velMin = na(ta.atr(30)) ? na : ta.atr(30) * velK

sub      = close - math.floor(close / 1000) * 1000
inMiddle = sub >= midLo and sub <= midHi

shortTrig = not na(p15h) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossunder(close, p15h) and (p15h - close) >= velMin

goShort = bearRegime and timeGate and h1Bear and brokeAbove and not inMiddle and shortTrig

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

shortR = shieldUsd

if flat and goShort and shortR > 0
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
    slPx   := close + shortR
    tpPx   := close - shortR * rr
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size < 0
    strategy.exit("SX", from_entry="S", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goShort ? 1 : 0, title="ShortSignal")
plot(redPrev,         title="PriorRed1hCount")
